<main class="landing">
  <header class="landing__hero">
    <p class="landing__eyebrow">Audra</p>
    <h1 class="landing__title">Your new Rails canvas</h1>
    <p class="landing__subhead">
      This is a simple landing page view you can reshape. Update the text, add sections,
      and wire up routes as your app grows.
    </p>
    <div class="landing__actions">
      <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/xyz">Try a new route</a>
      <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://guides.rubyonrails.org/">Rails guides</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="landing__grid">
    <div class="landing__card">
      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <p>Swap this content for your product pitch, onboarding, or pricing story.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="landing__card">
      <h2>Build fast</h2>
      <p>Add more routes and views as you go. Rails keeps it tidy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="landing__card">
      <h2>Go live</h2>
      <p>Deploy when ready. This page can become your marketing front door.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="landing__notes">
    <h2>What to edit</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Update the hero headline and subhead.</li>
      <li>Replace the cards with your own sections.</li>
      <li>Style the page in application.css.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
